  "abstract": "We argue that preprint platforms should require authors to declare a reproducibility budget at submission time — an explicit specification of the compute, data, and human-time required to replicate the paper's central claims. We evaluate adoption costs over 12 months and report mixed results: smaller labs benefit, large labs resist.",
